<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Airbnb hosts, guests and rooms: Inside Airbnb lakehouse results</title>
<meta name="description" content="Host portfolios, occupancy and revenue estimates, SCD2 price history, review velocity and licence compliance from Inside Airbnb snapshots.">
<style>
:root {
  --page: #f9f9f7; --surface-1: #fcfcfb; --ink: #0b0b0b; --ink-2: #52514e; --muted: #898781;
  --grid: #e1e0d9; --axis: #c3c2b7; --good: #006300; --bad: #d03b3b;
  --series-1: #2a78d6; --series-2: #eb6834; --series-3: #1baf7a; --series-4: #eda100;
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root {
    --page: #0d0d0d; --surface-1: #1a1a19; --ink: #ffffff; --ink-2: #c3c2b7; --muted: #898781;
    --grid: #2c2c2a; --axis: #383835; --good: #0ca30c; --bad: #e66767;
    --series-1: #3987e5; --series-2: #d95926; --series-3: #199e70; --series-4: #c98500;
  }
}
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
body { margin: 0; background: var(--page); color: var(--ink); font: 15px/1.5 system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif; }
main { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px 20px 64px; }
h1 { font-size: 1.7rem; margin: 0 0 4px; }
h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin: 40px 0 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--grid); padding-bottom: 6px; }
h3 { font-size: 1rem; margin: 20px 0 6px; }
p { margin: 6px 0; }
a { color: var(--series-1); }
.muted, .note { color: var(--ink-2); }
.note { font-size: .88rem; }
.badge { display: inline-block; font-size: .75rem; padding: 1px 7px; border-radius: 9px; border: 1px solid var(--axis); color: var(--ink-2); margin-left: 6px; vertical-align: middle; font-weight: 400; }
.cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr)); gap: 14px; margin-top: 14px; }
.card { background: var(--surface-1); border: 1px solid var(--grid); border-radius: 8px; padding: 14px 16px; }
.card h3 { margin: 0 0 2px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }
.card h3 i { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 2px; display: inline-block; }
.tiles { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 10px 12px; margin-top: 10px; }
.tile b { display: block; font-size: 1.3rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.tile span { font-size: .78rem; color: var(--ink-2); }
.tile em { font-style: normal; margin-left: 4px; }
.up { color: var(--good); } .down { color: var(--bad); }
.scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: .88rem; margin: 8px 0; background: var(--surface-1); }
th, td { padding: 5px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--grid); text-align: right; white-space: nowrap; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
th:first-child, td:first-child, td.l, th.l { text-align: left; }
th { color: var(--ink-2); font-weight: 600; }
.chart { width: 100%; height: auto; background: var(--surface-1); border-radius: 6px; }
.chart .grid { stroke: var(--grid); stroke-width: 1; }
.chart .tick { fill: var(--muted); font-size: 11px; }
.chart .direct { fill: var(--ink-2); font-size: 12px; }
.chart .pt { cursor: pointer; }
.legend { display: flex; gap: 16px; font-size: .85rem; color: var(--ink-2); margin: 8px 0; }
.legend .key i { display: inline-block; width: 12px; height: 3px; border-radius: 2px; margin-right: 6px; vertical-align: middle; }
#tip { position: fixed; pointer-events: none; background: var(--ink); color: var(--page); font-size: .8rem; padding: 4px 8px; border-radius: 4px; display: none; z-index: 10; }
details { margin: 8px 0; } summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--ink-2); }
.pass { color: var(--good); } .fail { color: var(--bad); font-weight: 600; }
footer { margin-top: 48px; font-size: .82rem; color: var(--ink-2); border-top: 1px solid var(--grid); padding-top: 12px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
<header>
  <h1>Airbnb hosts, guests and rooms</h1>
  <p class="muted">A batch lakehouse over <a href="https://insideairbnb.com/get-the-data/">Inside Airbnb</a> quarterly snapshots of
  {% for c in cities %}{{ c.name }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.
  Built {{ today }} from {{ summary.snapshots | length }} snapshots ({{ summary.snapshots | join(', ') }}).
  <a href="{{ repo_url }}">Source code</a>.</p>
  <p class="note">Every number on this page comes from the last pipeline run. The data is real. The AWS services in the design (S3, Glue,
  Athena, Step Functions) are <strong>emulated locally</strong> for this build. Occupancy, revenue and ADR are
  <strong>model estimates</strong>, not reported bookings. Prices are in each city's local currency, so cities are never summed.</p>
</header>

<section>
<h2>Latest snapshot by city</h2>
<div class="cards">
{% for c in cities %}
<div class="card">
  <h3><i style="background:var(--series-{{ loop.index }})"></i>{{ c.name }} <span class="badge">{{ c.date }}</span></h3>
  <p class="note">{{ c.country }}. Previous snapshot: {{ c.prev_date or '–' }}.</p>
  <div class="tiles">
    <div class="tile"><b>{{ c.listings | int }}</b><span>listings{% if c.listings_change is not none %}<em class="{{ 'up' if c.listings_change >= 0 else 'down' }}">{{ c.listings_change | spct }}</em>{% endif %}</span></div>
    <div class="tile"><b>{{ c.hosts | int }}</b><span>hosts</span></div>
    <div class="tile"><b>{{ c.entire_share | pct(0) }}</b><span>entire homes</span></div>
    <div class="tile"><b>{{ c.multi_host_listing_share | pct(0) }}</b><span>listings run by multi-listing hosts</span></div>
    <div class="tile"><b>{{ c.superhost_hosts | pct(0) }}</b><span>hosts who are Superhosts</span></div>
    <div class="tile"><b>{{ c.occ | pct(0) }}</b><span>est. occupancy (model)</span></div>
    <div class="tile"><b>{{ c.adr | money(c.sym) }}</b><span>est. ADR (model)</span></div>
    <div class="tile"><b>{{ c.median_rev | money(c.sym) }}</b><span>median est. revenue per listing, 12 months</span></div>
    <div class="tile"><b>{{ c.unlicensed_share | pct(0) }}</b><span>no licence text</span></div>
  </div>
</div>
{% endfor %}
</div>
</section>

<section>
<h2>Host portfolio</h2>
<p class="note">A host's portfolio is the number of their listings in that city's snapshot. "Multi-listing" means two or more.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table>
<tr><th class="l">City</th><th>Snapshot</th><th>Listings</th><th>Hosts</th><th>Single-listing hosts</th><th>Listings of multi-listing hosts</th><th>Listings of 10+ hosts</th><th>Superhosts (of hosts)</th><th>Superhosts (of listings)</th><th>New hosts</th><th>Departed hosts</th></tr>
{% for c in cities %}{% set h = d.hosts[(c.city, c.date)] %}
<tr><td>{{ c.name }}</td><td>{{ c.date }}</td><td>{{ h.listings | int }}</td><td>{{ h.hosts | int }}</td><td>{{ h.single_listing_host_share | pct }}</td><td>{{ h.multi_listing_host_listing_share | pct }}</td><td>{{ h.ten_plus_host_listing_share | pct }}</td><td>{{ h.superhost_share_of_hosts | pct }}</td><td>{{ h.superhost_share_of_listings | pct }}</td><td>{{ h.new_hosts | int }}</td><td>{{ h.departed_hosts | int }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table></div>
<h3>Largest portfolios (latest snapshot)</h3>
<p class="note">Hosts appear by rank and listing count only. Host names are not published here.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table>
<tr><th class="l">City</th><th>Rank</th><th>Listings</th><th>Entire homes</th><th>Private rooms</th><th>Other</th><th>Superhost</th></tr>
{% for t in d.top_hosts %}
<tr><td>{{ d.latest[t.city].city_name }}</td><td>{{ t.host_rank }}</td><td>{{ t.listings | int }}</td><td>{{ t.entire_homes | int }}</td><td>{{ t.private_rooms | int }}</td><td>{{ t.other_rooms | int }}</td><td>{{ 'yes' if t.is_superhost else 'no' }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table></div>
</section>

<section>
<h2>Occupancy, ADR and revenue <span class="badge">estimates</span></h2>
<p class="note">There are two separate measures. <strong>Calendar</strong>: the share of the next 30 nights that are not available. Airbnb's calendar
does not separate booked nights from nights the host blocked, so this is an upper bound. <strong>Occupancy model</strong>: Inside Airbnb's
"San Francisco model". Bookings = reviews in the last 12 months ÷ 0.5, because half of stays are assumed to leave a review. Nights per booking =
the larger of minimum nights and the city's average stay. Nights are capped at 255 a year (70%). Revenue = nights × listed price.
ADR = estimated revenue ÷ estimated booked nights, for listings with a price.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table>
<tr><th class="l">City</th><th>Average stay used</th><th>Next 30 nights unavailable</th><th>Highly available (&gt;90 nights/yr)</th><th>Est. occupancy</th><th>Frequently booked</th><th>Est. ADR</th><th>Est. RevPAL</th><th>Median est. revenue</th><th>Listings with a price</th></tr>
{% for c in cities %}
<tr><td>{{ c.name }}</td><td>{{ '%.1f' | format(c.avg_stay) }} nights</td><td>{{ c.unavail30 | pct }}</td><td>{{ c.highly_available | pct }}</td><td>{{ c.occ | pct }}</td><td>{{ c.frequently_booked | pct }}</td><td>{{ c.adr | money(c.sym) }}</td><td>{{ c.revpal | money(c.sym) }}</td><td>{{ c.median_rev | money(c.sym) }}</td><td>{{ c.priced_share | pct }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table></div>
</section>

<section>
<h2>Price change history <span class="badge">SCD Type 2</span></h2>
<p class="note">Each listing's price and tracked attributes are versioned across snapshots with dbt snapshots, replayed in snapshot order.
The history holds {{ d.scd2.versions | int }} versions of {{ d.scd2.listings | int }} listings, {{ d.scd2.current_versions | int }} of them currently open.
The changed share only counts listings that had a price in both snapshots.
<strong>Read with care:</strong> Inside Airbnb's price is the nightly rate quoted for one specific upcoming stay. In these snapshots the quote
is usually for the minimum stay and starts a few days after the scrape (median 1 to 13 days). So the price moves with seasonal and dynamic pricing,
and many "changes" reflect a different stay date rather than a host editing a list price.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table>
<tr><th class="l">City</th><th>Change window</th><th>Priced in both</th><th>Price up</th><th>Price down</th><th>Changed share</th><th>Median change</th><th>New listings</th><th>Delisted</th><th>Min-nights changes</th><th>Licence changes</th></tr>
{% for c in cities %}{% set p = c.price %}{% if p %}
<tr><td>{{ c.name }}</td><td>{{ p.previous_snapshot_date }} → {{ p.snapshot_date }}</td><td>{{ p.priced_in_both | int }}</td><td>{{ p.price_increases | int }}</td><td>{{ p.price_decreases | int }}</td><td>{{ p.price_changed_share | pct }}</td><td>{{ p.median_price_change_pct | spct }}</td><td>{{ p.new_listings | int }}</td><td>{{ p.delisted_listings | int }}</td><td>{{ p.minimum_nights_changes | int }}</td><td>{{ p.licence_changes | int }}</td></tr>
{% endif %}{% endfor %}
</table></div>
</section>

<section>
<h2>Review velocity</h2>
<p class="note">Reviews written per month, from each city's newest reviews file. That file only holds reviews of listings that are still listed,
so older months are undercounted. The current month is partial and is left out.</p>
{{ velocity_svg | safe }}
<details><summary>Table view</summary>
<div class="scroll"><table><tr><th class="l">Month</th><th class="l">City</th><th>Reviews</th><th>Year on year</th></tr>
{% for v in velocity_table %}<tr><td>{{ v.month.strftime('%Y-%m') }}</td><td class="l">{{ v.city }}</td><td>{{ v.reviews | int }}</td><td>{{ v.yoy | spct }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</table></div></details>
</section>

<section>
<h2>Guest sentiment <span class="badge">simple lexicon</span></h2>
<p class="note"><strong>Method:</strong> each review is scored by counting words from a short hand-written English word list
(72 positive and 66 negative words). There is no negation handling and no language model. Reviews in other languages mostly carry no signal.
Treat it as a rough trend indicator only. Covers the last 12 months of reviews.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table>
<tr><th class="l">City</th><th>Reviews</th><th>With a lexicon signal</th><th>Positive (of signalled)</th><th>Negative (of signalled)</th></tr>
{% for s in d.sentiment %}
<tr><td>{{ d.latest[s.city].city_name }}</td><td>{{ s.reviews | int }}</td><td>{{ s.coverage | pct }}</td><td>{{ s.positive_share | pct }}</td><td>{{ s.negative_share | pct }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table></div>
</section>

<section>
<h2>Neighbourhood supply (top 8 per city)</h2>
<div class="scroll"><table>
<tr><th class="l">City</th><th class="l">Neighbourhood</th><th>Listings</th><th>Share of city</th><th>Change vs previous</th><th>Entire homes</th><th>Multi-listing hosts</th><th>Median price</th></tr>
{% for n in d.neighbourhoods %}
<tr><td>{{ d.latest[n.city].city_name }}</td><td class="l">{{ n.neighbourhood }}</td><td>{{ n.listings | int }}</td><td>{{ n.share_of_city_listings | pct }}</td><td>{{ n.listings_change_pct | spct }}</td><td>{{ n.entire_home_share | pct(0) }}</td><td>{{ n.multi_host_listing_share | pct(0) }}</td><td>{{ n.median_price | money(d.latest[n.city].currency_symbol or '') }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table></div>
</section>

<section>
<h2>Licences and regulation <span class="badge">indicative</span></h2>
<p class="note">Licence status follows the Inside Airbnb dashboard rule: the field is empty, says exempt, says pending, or holds anything else
(counted as licensed). Nothing here checks whether a licence number is valid. The city rules are simplified and link to their sources.
A flag is not a legal finding.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table>
<tr><th class="l">City</th><th>Licensed</th><th>Unlicensed</th><th>Exempt</th><th>Pending</th><th class="l">Rule</th><th>In scope</th><th>Flagged</th><th>Flagged share</th></tr>
{% for r in d.compliance %}
<tr><td>{{ d.latest[r.city].city_name }}</td><td>{{ r.licensed | int }}</td><td>{{ r.unlicensed | int }}</td><td>{{ r.exempt | int }}</td><td>{{ r.pending | int }}</td>
<td class="l">{% if r.rule_id %}<a href="{{ r.rule_source_url }}" title="{{ r.rule_description }}">{{ r.rule_id }}</a>{% else %}–{% endif %}</td><td>{{ r.listings_in_scope | int }}</td><td>{{ r.listings_flagged | int }}</td><td>{{ r.flagged_share | pct }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table></div>
</section>

<section>
<h2>Verification against Inside Airbnb's own figures</h2>
{% if verification %}
{% set vs = verification.summary %}
<p class="note">{{ vs.dashboard_metrics_exact }} of {{ vs.dashboard_metrics_compared }} headline figures captured from the live city dashboards
match this build exactly. Captured for: {{ vs.cities_captured | join(', ') or 'none' }}. The mismatches are explained in docs/verification.md.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table>
<tr><th class="l">City</th><th>Snapshot</th><th class="l">Metric</th><th>Published</th><th>This build</th><th>Difference</th></tr>
{% for r in verification.dashboards %}
<tr><td>{{ r.city }}</td><td>{{ r.snapshot_date }}</td><td class="l">{{ r.metric }}</td><td>{{ r.published | int }}</td><td>{{ r.ours | int }}</td><td class="{{ 'pass' if r.match else 'fail' }}">{{ 'match' if r.match else (r.diff | int) }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table></div>
<h3>Our occupancy model compared with Inside Airbnb's published per-listing estimates</h3>
<div class="scroll"><table>
<tr><th class="l">City</th><th>Snapshot</th><th>Listings</th><th>Nights exactly equal</th><th>Within 10%</th><th>Our nights</th><th>Published nights</th></tr>
{% for r in verification.published_estimates %}
<tr><td>{{ r.city }}</td><td>{{ r.snapshot_date }}</td><td>{{ r.listings | int }}</td><td>{{ r.nights_exact_share | pct }}</td><td>{{ r.nights_within_10pct_share | pct }}</td><td>{{ r.our_nights | int }}</td><td>{{ r.published_nights | int }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table></div>
{% else %}
<p class="muted">No verification has been run for this build (<code>airbnb verify</code>).</p>
{% endif %}
</section>

<section>
<h2>Data-quality gates</h2>
<p class="note">A failed error-level check stops the pipeline before the next layer is built. Warnings are recorded but do not block.</p>
{% for layer, s in dq.items() %}{% if s %}
<details {% if s.errors_failed or s.warnings_failed %}open{% endif %}><summary><strong>{{ layer }}</strong>:
{{ s.results | length }} checks, <span class="{{ 'fail' if s.errors_failed else 'pass' }}">{{ s.errors_failed }} errors</span>, {{ s.warnings_failed }} warnings</summary>
<div class="scroll"><table><tr><th class="l">Check</th><th class="l">Severity</th><th>Violations</th><th class="l">Description</th></tr>
{% for r in s.results %}<tr><td class="l">{{ r.name }}</td><td class="l">{{ r.severity }}</td><td class="{{ 'pass' if r.passed else 'fail' }}">{{ r.violations | int }}</td><td class="l">{{ r.description }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</table></div></details>
{% endif %}{% endfor %}
</section>

<footer>
<p>Data: <a href="https://insideairbnb.com/">Inside Airbnb</a>, licensed under
<a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>. This page shows aggregates only.
This project has no connection to Airbnb or Inside Airbnb. Code: MIT. Generated {{ summary.generated_at }}; plan {{ summary.plan_fingerprint or '–' }}.</p>
</footer>
</main>
<div id="tip" role="status"></div>
<script>
(function () {
  var tip = document.getElementById('tip');
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-tip]').forEach(function (el) {
    el.addEventListener('mouseenter', function () { tip.textContent = el.getAttribute('data-tip'); tip.style.display = 'block'; });
    el.addEventListener('mousemove', function (e) { tip.style.left = (e.clientX + 12) + 'px'; tip.style.top = (e.clientY - 28) + 'px'; });
    el.addEventListener('mouseleave', function () { tip.style.display = 'none'; });
  });
})();
</script>
</body>
</html>
